<http://data.silknow.org/object/c2e675e8-1377-3a51-84a1-fba1f654633b/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Rectangular shan longyi weft-ikat cloth formed of two identical panels hand-stitched along the weft edge. The upper part is crossed by lines of yellow, pale-blue and red and white, on a light brown ground. The lower part has many horizontal bands, broad and narrow, decorated with a great variety of geometrically-treated motives including fret, hook, dot, cloud and floral motives, chiefly in white, purple and shades of green, yellow and red. Dyed silk woven in bands of geometric pattern of weft-ikat, plain weft and supplementary weft."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/c2e675e8-1377-3a51-84a1-fba1f654633b> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/c2e675e8-1377-3a51-84a1-fba1f654633b/domain/1>
